Three-part fix for the strategist -> exec-portal -> war-room confirmation chain:

1. construction-executive-portal.html: the AUTHORIZE button had no click
   handler at all, so TSM_EXEC_CONFIRMED_construction-suite was never
   written by any code path. Added tsmConfirmExec() wired to the button's
   onclick, writing the real (Convention A) unscoped key and flipping the
   button to AUTHORIZED once clicked.

2. construction-strategist.html: storeStrategistRelay() now writes the
   real TSM_STRAT_CONFIRMED_construction-suite key inline (previously
   only written by the dead tsmWriteScopedStrat(), which was never
   called anywhere in the repo). Removed that dead function. Also loads
   relay.core.js (already present on main) which was missing from this
   page's script includes. pushToSentinel() simplified to overwrite
   rather than merge/filter anomalies array (matches other verticals'
   pattern).

3. construction-war-room.html: status bar's strat/exec confirmation
   checks now fall back to scanning TSM_STRAT_CONFIRMED_construction-suite_*
   / TSM_EXEC_CONFIRMED_construction-suite_* scoped keys if the exact
   unscoped key isn't found, so the bar lights up regardless of which
   convention wrote the confirmation.

Isolated from feat/mission-preview-phase4 (194-file drift) — only these
3 files, no relay.core.js registry changes (Honeywell split / new domain
keys on that branch are unrelated and tracked separately).

Verified: server boots clean, all 3 pages + relay.core.js dependency
serve 200, onclick handler / dead-code removal / scoped-key fallback
all confirmed present in served output.
